      "message": "fix(notifications): unify push, local, and in-app tap routing (#4727) (#4736)\n\n* fix(notifications): unify push, local, and in-app tap routing (#4727)\n\nRoute all three notification tap entry points (FCM system push,\nlocal notification, and in-app rows) through one shared decision —\nresolveNotificationTapTarget — so they can no longer drift on where a\ntap lands, whether comments auto-open, or how unresolved targets fall\nback. The in-app executor keeps its existing screen + snackbar UX; only\nthe kind->destination decision is shared.\n\n- Follow & mention pushes no longer dead-end: the FCM payload's\n  senderPubkey is now parsed and carried through the local-notification\n  payload and NotificationTapEvent, and the push executor routes follows\n  (and unresolvable targets) to the actor profile or the inbox instead\n  of silently returning.\n- Comment auto-open is unified: the push path keyed off a 'reply' string\n  the service never sends (it sends lowercase 'comment'), so push\n  comments never auto-opened; now keyed off the shared policy.\n- Removes the dead NotificationPayloadKind.reply constant.\n\nContract verified against divine-push-service source: data-only FCM with\na lowercase five-value 'type' vocabulary plus senderPubkey.\n\n* fix(notifications): tighten tap-routing follow-up coverage\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Liz Sweigart <127434495+NotThatKindOfDrLiz@users.noreply.github.com>",
